  "body": "What changed\r\n- `assets/machines/sinker-edm.mch` ships in the library as \"Sinker EDM 3-axis (template)\". Its `edm` section is empty.\r\n- `posting::MACHINES` lists it. The only post that serves it is \"Sinker EDM (ISO)\".\r\n- `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` and `docs/decisions/1135-sinker-template-library.md` record the change.\r\n- The test fixture `crates/app/tests/edm/sinker-edm.mch` stays. A test pins that it equals the shipped file.\r\n- The ribbon has a sixth machine mode, \"Sinker EDM\". It mounts \"Sinker EDM 3-axis (template)\" with the same undoable `LoadBuiltinMachine` command as the other modes.\r\n- The `short_caption` catch-all arm is removed. Each machine kind now has its own arm.\r\n- Reason: main added a guard (issue 1501). The guard checks that each machine kind in the built-in library has a ribbon mode row.\r\n\r\nPinning tests\r\n- `sinker_burn::the_shipped_sinker_template_lists_and_refuses_its_unfilled_codes_by_name` (library entry, kind, post, refusal \"states no edm.codes.\").\r\n- `machine::every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration` now pins the new entry (an EDM kind is declared, never inferred).\r\n- `machine_mode_tests::the_sinker_template_has_its_own_mode_row` and `machine_mode_tests::every_kind_with_a_shipped_machine_has_a_mode` pin the new ribbon mode row.\r\n- `tips_match_the_imgui_table` pins the door tip of the Sinker row.\r\n\r\nTested\r\n- Suites that read `MACHINES`: 35 app test binaries pass. UI lib tests `machines_pane`, `setup_mount`, `machine_modes` pass. Clippy on camcraft-app tests is clean.\r\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: 816 passed. Clippy is clean on camcraft-app and camcraft-ui.\r\n- The full `cargo xtask gate quick` run was stopped by a timeout before the end. Only one failure showed (the pin above, now fixed).\r\n\r\nNot exercised\r\n- A real EDM control.\r\n- Nobody checked by eye that six ribbon tabs fit at the minimum window width.\r\n- The pixel-snapshot lanes and the `crates/ui/tests/` integration suites did not run. No snapshot PNG changed.\r\n- The full `cargo xtask gate quick` run did not complete on the final head.\r\n- MCP: no new command. The entry is listed through the existing machine tools.\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n\r\nHeadless render of the ribbon. Before: five machine tabs. After: six tabs, with \"Sinker EDM\" added.\r\n\r\nBefore, 1280 px wide:\r\n\r\n![before, 1280 px](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/0c546298e15c85ac69b092bc8326678fa905330f/pr-1753/before-1280.png?raw=true)\r\n\r\nAfter, 1280 px wide:\r\n\r\n![after, 1280 px](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/0c546298e15c85ac69b092bc8326678fa905330f/pr-1753/after-1280.png?raw=true)\r\n\r\nBefore, 1920 px wide:\r\n\r\n![before, 1920 px](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/0c546298e15c85ac69b092bc8326678fa905330f/pr-1753/before-1920.png?raw=true)\r\n\r\nAfter, 1920 px wide:\r\n\r\n![after, 1920 px](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/0c546298e15c85ac69b092bc8326678fa905330f/pr-1753/after-1920.png?raw=true)\r\n\r\nMachines pane, library list (headless render, 1280x800). The entry \"Sinker EDM 3-axis (template)\" shows with kind `sinker_edm`:\r\n\r\n![library list](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/b02c3572b1a0657cdfd456db37a0285e08df724c/pr-1753/machines-list-1280x800.png?raw=true)\r\n\r\nMachines pane with the sinker template selected. The sheet says \"Validation: passes\" and shows an empty EDM setup:\r\n\r\n![sinker selected](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/b02c3572b1a0657cdfd456db37a0285e08df724c/pr-1753/machines-sinker-selected-1280x800.png?raw=true)\r\n\r\nNote: the kind filter of the pane offers only Mill, Lathe, Mill-turn and Plasma. It has no EDM kind. This is not part of this PR.\r\n\r\nHead c545e5fcd (main merged, no conflict). Re-run on this head: `camcraft-app` tests `sinker_burn` (33 passed) and `machine` (15 passed); `camcraft-ui --lib machine` (80 passed); clippy on `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-ui` with `--tests -D warnings` clean.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Sinker EDM template joins the built-in machine library (#1135)\r\nEffort: medium\r\n\r\nFixes #1135\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\r\n",
